From c372c876d9025840d318b7016ffb5bb9664fdaca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Manuel Klimek <klimek@box4.net>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 20:43:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wayland: forward pointer lock to host compositor when running
 nested

When kwin runs nested inside another Wayland compositor, pointer lock
requests from clients were not forwarded to the host compositor. This
caused the cursor to escape the window in applications relying on
relative mouse input, such as games running via Proton.

Add a pointerLockStateChanged signal to PointerInputRedirection, emitted
whenever a client acquires or releases a pointer lock. Connect it in
WaylandInputBackend::initialize() so WaylandBackend can lock/unlock the
pointer on the host compositor and enable relative pointer events for the
duration of the lock.

Add integration tests verifying that the signal fires on lock state
transitions and that relative motion events are forwarded to clients
while the pointer is locked.
